WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.436 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.505
-Cheers, everybody.
How about this? 50.

00:00:06.505 --> 00:00:08.708
This is 50 "Corrections."

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.110
-If you had told me
when we started

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.112
that we would do
50 "Corrections,"

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:17.650
I would have said, "Yeah, I
guess so. I mean, why not?

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.485
I mean, I'm the only one
who does anything."

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:22.856
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.258
Like, I like it.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.894
Hey, I said the Jackal
was an acronym for.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.596
Jerks Attempting Comedy-Killing
Absent Love.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.865
And I was told
that's a "back-cronym,"

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:36.202
which is when you create
an acronym based on

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.804
an existing word.

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:41.407
Basically someone said
that I deliberately

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:43.042
worked Backwards from Jackal.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:46.779
That's not how it happened.

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:48.748
You remember, Shoemaker -- I
came -- I went in --

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.283
The first time
I read any of your comments,

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:53.285
marched right over
to Shoemaker's office,

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:55.421
and I said,
I got a bunch of jerks

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.090
attempting comedy,
killing absent love.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.794
And then you were
the one who was like, "Oh."

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:04.464
And remember?
And then I went, "Oh."

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:07.599
And then you were like,
"Oh-oh-oh."

00:01:07.599 --> 00:01:09.835
And then I said, "Ah!"

00:01:09.835 --> 00:01:16.342
And that's how
we came up with it.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:21.381
My favorite thing this week is
someone by accident --

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:23.583
On accident --
Let me know.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:28.087
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:34.527
If someone accidentally...called
Shoemaker, "butter maker."

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:39.165
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:43.169
Which is funny because
"Butter Maker" is his alter ego.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:46.239
-Because Shoemaker used to --
not any more after the leg.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:50.342
But Shoemaker used to drink
and black out.

00:01:50.342 --> 00:01:52.778
And then the next day you'd go
in his office and [Bleep]

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:55.114
would be off the walls and you
say, "What happened?"

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:57.216
He goes, "I think
Butter Maker was here."

00:01:57.216 --> 00:02:00.353
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.655
"Oops."
He doesn't really --

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:04.290
[ Laughs ]

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.658
Oops!

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:10.697
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:15.335
Speaking of butter maker,
if you think 1976 is

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:18.338
bad news bears is a movie
you can show kids today.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:21.874
I got some bad news, Bears.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:26.346
I don't even think
you can show them the trailer.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:30.249
Oh, I said -- I referred to
somebody bringing a turntable

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:33.052
to a party as being a deejay.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.888
I was told
by a bunch of people

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:39.324
that if someone shows up
with one turntable

00:02:39.324 --> 00:02:40.960
they are not a deejay.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.463
So don't let
that person into your house.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:47.667
If they show up with two
turntables and a mixer,

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.168
Then they are a deejay.

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:51.571
And don't let that person
into your house.

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:55.374
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:59.078
The Titanic was a ship,
I referred to it as a boat.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.947
On the upside,
not the worst thing

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:02.849
that happened to the Titanic.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:08.387
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:11.824
"The New York Times" Mini.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:15.061
The mini crossword puzzle,
a lot of you brought this

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:20.099
to my attention
and this as an answer.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.701
Plastic toy, bricks.
And the answer is Legos.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.036
Well, I don't need to tell you.

00:03:24.036 --> 00:03:26.839
I mean, we, we set off on this
journey of 50 episodes

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:30.342
when we were told
there's no plural for Legos.

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:34.013
You say Lego bricks.
Legos is incorrect.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:37.684
But, you know, I would just say
to the to the Jackals out there,

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.685
you know, don't be --
it's just a mini.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.688
Don't beat up on the mini.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:45.057
"The New York Times" Mini
is interesting.

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:48.628
It is -- It's for people
who love puzzles.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:51.030
But hate impressing people.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.466
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.466 --> 00:04:00.472
Do you get the Mini today?

00:04:00.472 --> 00:04:03.376
I mentioned Tintin.

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:05.711
Told I was
pronouncing it wrong.

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:07.346
Tintin is the Americanization.

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:09.949
In French,
you say, "Tonton."

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:13.452
That did -- It does seem a
little weird to my ear

00:04:13.452 --> 00:04:15.955
to say "Tonton,"
after all these years.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:21.060
But again, as fortune has it,
there is a person in my life

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.529
who is perfect to ask about
English versus French.

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.898
So I reached out
to my mom and asked

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:30.770
how she would say the
little boy, the, the traveler,

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.805
the journalist extraordinaire.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.840
Mom, how would you say it?

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.610
-Kahn, kahn!
-Kahn-kahn.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:44.750
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:49.388
Hey, this was,
this was again, this was a

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:55.194
Jackals joke and I gave credit
about Nosfera-Chews--

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.329
the delicious candy.

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:59.732
And you know,
because I gave credit,

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:04.136
correctly,
the Jackals were celebrating

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:05.404
in the comment section
this week

00:05:05.404 --> 00:05:10.175
That one of their own
had, had, had busted out.

00:05:10.175 --> 00:05:13.913
And these were the, these
were the three comments

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:18.184
after someone said they
used my joke.

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:21.520
First person said, "The
Nosfera-Chews swelled feelings

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.790
of pride for the contributing
Jackal, well done."

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:28.961
Second person, "Nosfera-Chews
was major league funny.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:32.031
You may make the bigs kid."
Very sweet.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:34.833
Third one, "His name
isn't Nosfera-Chew, though.

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:36.903
Nosferatu, though
it's Count Orlok.

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.405
Nosferatu is the name
of the movie."

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:44.343
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:46.712
And so for the Jackal,
who wrote that joke,

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:50.516
welcome to the roller coaster
that is my life.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:55.254
Write a good joke, praise,
praise, Jackal ruins day.

00:05:59.191 --> 00:06:00.593
It is right, though.

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:03.296
The character in Nosferatu,
the original one,

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:08.567
the F.W. Murnau was Count Orlok,
which I remembered,

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:11.370
because in the '80s
General Mills did a

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:16.175
German Expressionism serial
crossover and released this --

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:18.144
Count Chorlokula.

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:23.883
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:26.419
I believe the term for it
is short lived.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:38.297
Hey, uh, I want to apologize to
a couple of hot sauce companies,

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:41.099
Tabasco and Cholula.

00:06:41.099 --> 00:06:42.935
During -- We went day drinking,
I went day drinking

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:46.171
with Post Malone and
there were two great hot sauces.

00:06:46.171 --> 00:06:50.209
And while I was shaking out
the Cholula,

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:52.912
I called it Tabasco.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:54.747
In my defense,
and there's no way anyone

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:59.085
watching that could have known
this, I had been drinking.

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:00.820
[ Laughter ]

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:10.863
We did a sketch called, uh,
"Best Case, Worst Case,"

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:13.166
which was had a lot of
bee content --

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:16.102
Content based on the insect.

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:18.637
More commonly known
as the Bee.

00:07:18.637 --> 00:07:21.741
And. well,
there were some problems.

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:24.243
First there was the line
first graphics had an issue,

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:28.014
which we said, uh,
bees blotted out the Sun.

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:30.983
And, you know, when when
anything blots out the Sun,

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:33.385
the idea is that
they cover the sky.

00:07:33.385 --> 00:07:35.554
There are so many of them
the sky, you can't see the Sun.

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:39.625
Whereas graphics thought bees
just swarmed to the sun.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:43.395
And, like, landed on it.

00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:45.665
However you want to think that,
because, of course,

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:47.399
that wouldn't,
as a lot of you pointed out,

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:52.238
the bees would, you know,
they would, they'd incinerate.

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:58.444
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:01.747
Jermaine wrote -- our writer
Jermaine wrote this sketch

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:07.220
and he's a -- he's usually got
a good attention to detail.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.922
Now, again, in his defense.

00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:13.859
I think the first draft of this
was only written 18 months ago.

00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:16.762
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:16.762 --> 00:08:20.666
So there wasn't a ton
of time, you know.

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:24.269
Dot the I's and cross the T's.

00:08:24.269 --> 00:08:25.904
So there were a few --

00:08:25.904 --> 00:08:27.973
There were a few of you
who knew a little bit more

00:08:27.973 --> 00:08:30.876
about bees than anybody --
it was just a few.

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:33.945 line:0%
Male bees don't have stingers,
that's one.

00:08:33.945 --> 00:08:36.181 line:0%
When the queen dies,
the drones don't also die,

00:08:36.181 --> 00:08:38.183 line:0%
they rear a new queen.

00:08:38.183 --> 00:08:39.819 line:0%
[ Bees buzz ]

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:47.660 line:0%
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.762 line:0%
Bees don't die when they lose
their stingers that's wasps.

00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:51.430 line:0%
That's three.
[ Bees buzz ]

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:52.731 line:0%
Bees don't say "buzz"
that's the sound

00:08:52.731 --> 00:08:54.333 line:0%
their wings make when they fly.
That's four.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.669 line:0%
[ Bees buzz ]
Queen bees can't five -- fly.

00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:58.503 line:0%
Five. [ Laughs ]
[ Bees buzz ]

00:08:58.503 --> 00:09:01.173 line:0%
You showed a picture
of a wasp not a bee.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:02.307 line:0%
[ Bees buzz ]

00:09:02.307 --> 00:09:03.876 line:0%
Bees would be able to blot out
the Sun --

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:05.411 line:0%
Oh, not just because they
wouldn't blot out the Sun,

00:09:05.411 --> 00:09:07.513 line:0%
they can't survive in space.
That's seven. Yeah.

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:10.549 line:0%
[ Bees buzz ]

00:09:10.549 --> 00:09:12.484 line:0%
And then the final correction
was one that really

00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:15.387 line:0%
wasn't even bee related about
this wonderful sketch

00:09:15.387 --> 00:09:17.923 line:0%
that Jermaine wrote.

00:09:17.923 --> 00:09:21.260 line:0%
Correction, this was not
supposed to air.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:29.936 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:35.307
You know, I mentioned that we
don't get a lot of fan art

00:09:35.307 --> 00:09:37.843
and I think a lot of you took
it the wrong way.

00:09:37.843 --> 00:09:39.345
I don't remember saying this
because, you know, again,

00:09:39.345 --> 00:09:42.180
I was fishing for it,
but I guess a lot of you

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:45.618
heard we don't get a lot
of Wally fan art.

00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:48.053
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:48.053 --> 00:09:50.722
I don't know what it is about
Wally, but people are,

00:09:50.722 --> 00:09:52.892
people are drawn to him.

00:09:52.892 --> 00:09:56.595
-You know.
-Maybe he's born with it.

00:09:56.595 --> 00:09:58.197
"Maybe it's Wabelline."

00:09:58.197 --> 00:10:04.403
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.074 --> 00:10:10.443
We talked about Wally "Two
Trees" Feresten

00:10:10.443 --> 00:10:12.711
and, and and this meme
that somebody made.

00:10:12.711 --> 00:10:14.013
And there were two things
that were pointed out to me

00:10:14.013 --> 00:10:15.381
that I got to say are fair,
one

00:10:15.381 --> 00:10:17.816
while he's holding the cue card
that says Seth sucks.

00:10:17.816 --> 00:10:19.685
Someone said,
But you read what he says.

00:10:19.685 --> 00:10:21.519
So technically it should say,
"I suck."

00:10:21.519 --> 00:10:23.622
I think that's right,
but would have been confusing.

00:10:23.622 --> 00:10:26.324
Also, someone said, "At no point
would I have said that

00:10:26.324 --> 00:10:29.061
Tony Soprano's nickname was
'Da Boss.'"

00:10:29.061 --> 00:10:38.770
[ Laughter ]

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.339
And then someone said
they came up

00:10:40.339 --> 00:10:43.642
with a better nickname for Wally
than Wally Two Trees Feresten.

00:10:43.642 --> 00:10:46.545
And I love
Wally Two Trees Feresten.

00:10:46.545 --> 00:10:48.580
And I thought, I bet you don't.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.082
And then they told me.

00:10:50.082 --> 00:10:53.151
And I will say,
I laughed when I read it.

00:10:53.151 --> 00:10:54.353
Wally Paulnuts.

00:10:54.353 --> 00:11:04.296
[ Laughter ]

00:11:04.296 --> 00:11:07.499
They also said
Mike "Tank-top" Scollins.

00:11:07.499 --> 00:11:09.668
It should be if you have no, no
trees, it should be

00:11:09.668 --> 00:11:12.104
Mike "No-sleeves" Scollins.

00:11:12.104 --> 00:11:14.006
We had a pretty great crew.

00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:20.846
Mikey No-sleeves,
Butter Maker, Wally Paulnuts,

00:11:20.846 --> 00:11:25.651
and Jermaine "Refuses
To Google Bee Facts."

00:11:25.651 --> 00:11:29.488
We called him that because he
refused to Google bee facts.

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:33.425
[ Light laughter ]

00:11:33.425 --> 00:11:38.030
Speaking of speaking
of no sleeves, Scollins,

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:41.967
he had a joke about
a Guinness World Record

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:46.972
being set for the largest
chicken nugget ever made.

00:11:46.972 --> 00:11:50.342
That was the setup.
To put it in joke parlance.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:55.114
[ Laughter ]

00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:57.817
And then the punch line
was and now for the bad news.

00:11:57.817 --> 00:12:01.486
And we showed a picture
of Big Bird.

00:12:01.486 --> 00:12:05.624
And many of you took offense,
and many more of you said,

00:12:05.624 --> 00:12:08.727
"Big Bird is a canary,
not a chicken.

00:12:08.727 --> 00:12:12.131
So the joke doesn't work."

00:12:12.131 --> 00:12:15.968
Because if there's one thing we
know, chicken nuggets

00:12:15.968 --> 00:12:18.337
[As Big Bird]
only have chicken.

00:12:18.337 --> 00:12:27.212
[ Laughter ]

00:12:27.212 --> 00:12:29.114
[ Normal voice ]
This is just a genuine question

00:12:29.114 --> 00:12:33.385
I have to our our European --
our international viewers.

00:12:33.385 --> 00:12:37.489
Talked about the sexy
firefighter calendar and how

00:12:37.489 --> 00:12:40.893
it started on Monday
and calendars start on Sunday.

00:12:40.893 --> 00:12:43.294
But it seems like,
everywhere but America,

00:12:43.294 --> 00:12:44.997
they start on Monday.

00:12:44.997 --> 00:12:47.199
So people said you were fine,
you didn't need to correct that.

00:12:47.199 --> 00:12:50.236
The question I have is,
does the rest of the world

00:12:50.236 --> 00:12:52.571
have sexy firefighter calendars?

00:12:58.043 --> 00:13:00.979
We'll post a poll.

00:13:00.979 --> 00:13:04.783
Don't answer if you're not from
out of the country.

00:13:04.783 --> 00:13:08.920
Doesn't work
and we stop taking it seriously.

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:13.258
Oh, I talked about Paul Revere
charging for his midnight ride,

00:13:13.258 --> 00:13:15.160
you know, because he had
all these expenses,

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:17.763
like he was using his own horse.
and a bunch of you said,

00:13:17.763 --> 00:13:21.099
not only do you not use his own
horse, he borrowed a horse

00:13:21.099 --> 00:13:22.300
and he never brought it back.

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:25.938
So I guess Paul Revere
is canceled now.

00:13:25.938 --> 00:13:28.607
[ Laughter ]

00:13:28.607 --> 00:13:30.609
When does it stop?

00:13:40.085 --> 00:13:41.520
Pizza Hut.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.322
Our friends at Pizza Hut, they
sent they sent us free pizza

00:13:44.322 --> 00:13:47.392
today for our staff
and our crew.

00:13:47.392 --> 00:13:48.994
Such a nice gesture --
Also this week,

00:13:48.994 --> 00:13:53.132
Little Caesars replaced
Pizza Hut as the official pizza

00:13:53.132 --> 00:13:54.566
of the NFL.

00:13:54.566 --> 00:14:00.005
And I just pray those.
two aren't related.

00:14:00.005 --> 00:14:02.541
That someone at Pizza Hut said,
"I'd love to send pizza to

00:14:02.541 --> 00:14:05.110
the team over at 'Late Night'"
and then, you know, their boss

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.413
said, "Okay, but you gotta find
the money somewhere else.

00:14:07.413 --> 00:14:10.415
[ Laughter ]

00:14:10.415 --> 00:14:11.616
Because that's what
I'm hoping, right?

00:14:11.616 --> 00:14:15.186
I'm hoping that Pizza Hut
opted out

00:14:15.186 --> 00:14:17.957
of being the official pizza
of the NFL.

00:14:17.957 --> 00:14:19.291
I don't know the story about it,

00:14:19.291 --> 00:14:23.429
but I'd hate to think
they were still trying to.

00:14:23.429 --> 00:14:28.300
Look, I just don't want to
live in a world

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:32.304
where they got out pizza'd.

00:14:32.304 --> 00:14:40.813
[ Laughter ]

00:14:40.813 --> 00:14:42.648
But maybe that's what --
maybe they opted out.

00:14:42.648 --> 00:14:44.783
Because they want --
they are over the official pizza

00:14:44.783 --> 00:14:47.719
of the NFL maybe they want to be
the official

00:14:47.719 --> 00:14:50.054
pizza of "Corrections."

00:14:50.054 --> 00:14:51.357
We're in talks.

00:14:51.357 --> 00:14:54.359
[ Laughter ]

00:14:54.359 --> 00:14:55.694
And I don't think
we have the reach.

00:14:55.694 --> 00:14:58.663
I'm not going to sit here and
lie to you and say

00:14:58.663 --> 00:15:01.399
we've got the reach or
the scope of the NFL.

00:15:01.399 --> 00:15:04.003
But let me say something,
50 episodes.

00:15:04.003 --> 00:15:06.739
50 episodes, not one concussion.

00:15:06.739 --> 00:15:10.308
[ Laughter ]

00:15:10.308 --> 00:15:11.911
And we go hard.

00:15:14.946 --> 00:15:17.849
Remember that movie
"Concussion"?

00:15:17.849 --> 00:15:21.020
Where there was a doctor who
taught everybody

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:27.927
The trauma one could receive
with with a blow to the head.

00:15:27.927 --> 00:15:29.528
How traumatic
a blow to the head --

00:15:29.528 --> 00:15:32.631
Do you remember who played
the doctor? Will Smith.

00:15:32.631 --> 00:15:38.804
Foreshadowing.

00:15:38.804 --> 00:15:44.175
Oh, by the way, I knew about
the Little Caesars news,

00:15:44.175 --> 00:15:48.480
because of there was
a PR press release.

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.582
My PR was public relations.

00:15:53.418 --> 00:15:56.087
They had this press release
from Little Caesars

00:15:56.087 --> 00:15:58.957
explaining how they're and, and
I think we can all agree

00:15:58.957 --> 00:16:00.826
just by looking at it, too long.

00:16:00.826 --> 00:16:09.734
[ Laughter ]

00:16:09.734 --> 00:16:13.939
Oh, I was told that people
from Queens never say Queens.

00:16:13.939 --> 00:16:16.608
They would say "Astoria"
or "Long Island."

00:16:16.608 --> 00:16:17.843
But I just want to say
to all of them.

00:16:17.843 --> 00:16:20.345
Behind your back,
we say Queens.

00:16:20.345 --> 00:16:24.916
♪♪

00:16:24.916 --> 00:16:27.252
Someone said, "Your
O.J. impression was terrible."

00:16:27.252 --> 00:16:29.922
Well, I'll make sure to
lean into it next time.

00:16:29.922 --> 00:16:35.461
[ Laughter ]

00:16:40.165 --> 00:16:44.169
Hey,

00:16:44.169 --> 00:16:48.740
when I think we're a month out
from getting the merch.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.709
Here's the thing,
when the merch is ready,

00:16:50.709 --> 00:16:53.879
you guys got to buy the merch,
okay?

00:16:53.879 --> 00:16:56.615
I've been making a big deal
about the merch

00:16:56.615 --> 00:16:59.017
and I'm calling up the merch
people and making a stink

00:16:59.017 --> 00:17:01.887
every day and if you guys don't
buy the merch,

00:17:01.887 --> 00:17:04.022
I'm not going to be able
to look them in the eye

00:17:04.022 --> 00:17:07.526
when I see them at the
commissary, buy the merch.

00:17:07.526 --> 00:17:09.762
If I go down to
the NBC Experience Store

00:17:09.762 --> 00:17:11.463
and the merch
is in the discount bin

00:17:11.463 --> 00:17:14.733
with the you know, "Where in the
World is Matt Lauer"

00:17:14.733 --> 00:17:24.443
beer cozies --
[ Laughter ]

00:17:28.914 --> 00:17:31.616
Um, I want to read a comment.

00:17:31.616 --> 00:17:33.886
Someone left a comment,
a critical comment,

00:17:33.886 --> 00:17:37.155
but it made me think and --

00:17:37.155 --> 00:17:40.692
Again, this whole thing,
all jokes aside,

00:17:40.692 --> 00:17:42.327
it is about improvement.

00:17:42.327 --> 00:17:45.264
I want to be better. and I
appreciate the time

00:17:45.264 --> 00:17:47.365
all of you Jackals take to
engage with the show.

00:17:47.365 --> 00:17:48.734
I hope you know that.

00:17:48.734 --> 00:17:51.136
Every now and then maybe I come
off as a little surly.

00:17:51.136 --> 00:17:54.739
But you take time,
I take the time to read them.

00:17:54.739 --> 00:17:56.874
I think we both
come out of it better.

00:17:56.874 --> 00:17:58.676
So this is a critical comment
and I want to read it

00:17:58.676 --> 00:18:01.180
'cause it made me think
and I'm going to read it --

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.248
I'm going to use a voice
when I read it.

00:18:03.248 --> 00:18:05.650
And I don't want you
to think the voice is me

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:08.386
editorializing about
the comment.

00:18:08.386 --> 00:18:13.291
The voice I use is completely
unconnected to how I feel

00:18:13.291 --> 00:18:16.961
about what you took
the time to write, okay?

00:18:16.961 --> 00:18:18.963
[Strange British-like voice]
The less political relevance

00:18:18.963 --> 00:18:23.135
this show has the less funny
and interesting it becomes.

00:18:23.135 --> 00:18:26.771
"Corrections" is always a word
salad of unfunny, puns,

00:18:26.771 --> 00:18:28.974
quirky nonsense

00:18:28.974 --> 00:18:31.309
that amounts to obnoxious
Internet banter

00:18:31.309 --> 00:18:34.513
and nothing more.

00:18:34.513 --> 00:18:38.450
Can't you correct
the Republican Party?

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:41.686
Or something worthwhile?

00:18:41.686 --> 00:18:43.221
This is so meaningless,

00:18:43.221 --> 00:18:45.223
it makes me not laugh
again and again.

00:18:45.223 --> 00:18:47.092
[ Normal voice ]
So just thank you.

00:18:47.092 --> 00:18:49.294
[ Laughter ]

00:18:49.294 --> 00:18:53.332
Taking the time to write
something so important.

00:18:53.332 --> 00:18:55.701
Um --

00:18:55.701 --> 00:19:00.104
This is a, this is 50,
but next week is the

00:19:00.104 --> 00:19:05.310
this -- the spec-jack-ular
jack-tacular?

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:07.679
We'll have, uh...

00:19:07.679 --> 00:19:10.215
Let's have Peacock
do some market research.

00:19:10.215 --> 00:19:13.418
"Jack-tacular"
or "Spec-jack-ular"?

00:19:13.418 --> 00:19:17.889
And it's, it's gonna be big.

00:19:17.889 --> 00:19:19.791
[ Light laughter ]

00:19:19.791 --> 00:19:21.392
It's gonna be
really, really big.

00:19:21.392 --> 00:19:23.629
It's, um, we are um...

00:19:25.797 --> 00:19:28.967
We spent a lot of money on it.

00:19:28.967 --> 00:19:32.070
And I think when you tune in,
you're going to be blown away.

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:33.438
Right off the jump.

00:19:33.438 --> 00:19:35.440
There is...
you know, obviously,

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:38.009
we no longer use live
animals on the show.

00:19:38.009 --> 00:19:41.579
So that, that whole element
of it has to be CGI.

00:19:42.146 --> 00:19:44.115
[ Light laughter ]

00:19:44.115 --> 00:19:47.486
Rehearsals, whew.

00:19:47.486 --> 00:19:50.188
The rehearsals are intense.

00:19:50.188 --> 00:19:55.961
So do, do please come back in a
week for that.

00:19:55.961 --> 00:19:59.064
But thank you for being here
for the 50th.

00:19:59.064 --> 00:20:03.401
I think this was by far, you
know, Top 25.

00:20:03.401 --> 00:20:05.837
[ Light laughter ]

00:20:05.837 --> 00:20:11.410
You, will see me next week.

